      },
      "finding": null,
      "explanation": "Several code examples perform destructive, irreversible file-write operations (e.g., merging, splitting, rotating, encrypting PDFs) without any guidance to confirm with the user or warn about overwriting existing files. For instance, the merge example writes to 'merged.pdf' and the split example writes to 'page_{i+1}.pdf' with hardcoded names that could silently overwrite existing files. An agent following this code could destroy user data without warning.",
      "remediation": "Add explicit guidance in the skill documentation to: (1) always use user-supplied output paths, (2) check for existing files before writing and prompt for confirmation, (3) prefer writing to temporary locations first, then moving on user confirmation. Include a note warning that these operations can overwrite existing files.",
      "code_snippet": null,
      "intent": null,
      "tags": []
    },
    {
      "id": "SQP-2",
      "finding_id": "finding-1b47de4746ad492eb33a1e5e51a8bbc4",
