        "end_line": 216
      },
      "finding": null,
      "explanation": "The skill provides a qpdf command example that decrypts a password-protected PDF using a supplied password and writes the result to an unencrypted file, with no warning about the sensitivity of this operation. An agent could strip encryption from confidential documents without adequately warning the user about the implications \u2014 such as the decrypted file being stored in plaintext on disk, potentially in a world-readable location. This could expose sensitive content if performed without explicit informed consent.",
      "remediation": "Add a prominent warning before any decryption example stating that: (1) the output file will be permanently unencrypted, (2) the user should ensure the output path is secure, (3) the operation should only proceed after explicit user confirmation. Consider requiring the skill to always prompt for confirmation before executing decryption operations.",
      "code_snippet": null,
      "intent": null,
      "tags": []
    },
    {
      "id": "SDI-2",
      "finding_id": "finding-1a1a2eaaae85470d855a4d3cf561a183",
