        "file": "forms.md",
        "start_line": 195,
        "end_line": 207
      },
      "finding": null,
      "explanation": "The skill instructs the AI agent to invoke shell commands using ImageMagick (`magick` or `convert`) directly as part of its workflow for visual estimation of form fields. While the primary intent is clearly functional (cropping PDF page images for coordinate refinement), this pattern creates a pathway for shell command execution with user-controlled input (file paths, dimensions) interpolated directly into the command string. A malicious user could craft a PDF filename or parameter containing shell metacharacters (e.g., semicolons, backticks, pipe characters) that get passed unsanitized to the shell, resulting in arbitrary command execution on the host system.",
      "remediation": "1. Sanitize and validate all user-supplied inputs (filenames, dimensions, offsets) before interpolating them into shell commands. 2. Use argument arrays rather than shell strings when invoking subprocesses (e.g., Python's `subprocess.run([...], shell=False)`). 3. Restrict allowed characters in filenames to an allowlist (alphanumerics, hyphens, underscores, dots). 4. Consider wrapping ImageMagick calls inside a dedicated Python script that handles argument validation, rather than exposing raw shell command templates to the AI agent.",
      "code_snippet": null,
      "intent": null,
      "tags": []
    },
    {
      "id": "SQP-2",
      "finding_id": "finding-57ef988bb6c04977b9fe2ae39c638ef9",
